\section{Why these seven and not right/wrong}{

The costly outcomes are not symmetric, and collapsing them hides the two the
pipeline most needs to count. \code{FALSE_MATCH} is a reviewer naming an EIN where
the truth table says no organisation exists at all — an individual payee, a
government body, a payee with no exemption of its own — which
\code{\link[=pf_evaluate]{pf_evaluate()}} already treats as an unambiguous false accept for a run.
\code{RULED_OUT} is narrower and worse than \code{WRONG_EIN}: adjudication had already
excluded that specific EIN, so the review contradicts a recorded negative
rather than merely missing.

\code{UNSCOREABLE} exists so that an unscoreable case cannot be silently counted
as wrong. A truth row of \code{UNRESOLVED}, or a \code{MATCH} against a row with
neither a \code{correct_ein} nor a \code{wrong_ein}, carries no answer to compare with;
\code{is_correct} is \code{NA} on those rows and every denominator below excludes them.
}

